  "ansi": "\u001b[2m~/src/app\u001b[0m $ agentbus demo | cat\r\nagentbus demo: two agents on a temporary bus, about 30 seconds. Nothing here touches your project.\r\n(The bus lives in /tmp/agentbus-demo-n7jfjsl3 and is removed when the tour ends.)\r\n\r\n# Two agents join the bus. Each names itself with --as.\r\n$ agentbus --as lead join --role planner\r\njoined as lead on /tmp/agentbus-demo-n7jfjsl3/bus/bus.db\r\n$ agentbus --as worker join --role implementer --tool codex\r\njoined as worker on /tmp/agentbus-demo-n7jfjsl3/bus/bus.db\r\n\r\n# The lead sets the one goal every agent sees first.\r\n$ agentbus --as lead goal 'Move auth to the new token API'\r\ngoal: Move auth to the new token API\r\n\r\n# The lead posts the task to the worker.\r\n$ agentbus --as lead post 'Move src/auth/ onto the new token API.' --to worker\r\nposted #1 to worker [note]\r\n\r\n# The worker reads its inbox.\r\n$ agentbus --as worker inbox\r\n#1 lead -> worker [note] · 01:54\r\n  Move src/auth/ onto the new token API.\r\n\r\n# The worker claims the folder before it edits.\r\n$ agentbus --as worker claim src/auth/ --purpose 'token refactor'\r\nclaimed src/auth/ for 2h (until 03:54)\r\n\r\n# The lead tries to edit a file inside it. The claim is refused, which is the point.\r\n$ agentbus --as lead claim src/auth/login.py --purpose 'quick fix'\r\nagentbus: src/auth/login.py overlaps src/auth/, claimed by worker until 03:54 (purpose: \"token refactor\"). Do not edit it yet. Ask worker: agentbus --as lead post QUESTION --to worker --kind question, or choose another resource. worker was last seen just now.\r\n\r\n# The worker finishes and hands off.\r\n$ agentbus --as worker post 'Auth is moved and tests pass. Over to you for review.' --to lead --kind handoff\r\nposted #2 to lead [handoff]\r\n\r\n# Any agent can catch up in one call.\r\n$ agentbus --as lead brief\r\ngoal: Move auth to the new token API (set by lead)\r\nhere (2):\r\n  lead (planner), now\r\n  worker (implementer, codex), now, holds src/auth/ [token refactor]\r\nopen questions: none\r\nunread handoffs and alerts (1):\r\n  #2 worker [handoff]: Auth is moved and tests pass. Over to you for review.\r\npending between others: none\r\nfacts: none\r\nnext: agentbus --as lead inbox\r\n\r\n# The worker lets go of the folder.\r\n$ agentbus --as worker release src/auth/\r\nreleased src/auth/\r\n\r\nThat was the whole loop, and the demo bus is already gone. To use it in your own repo:\r\n  agentbus init .\r\n  agentbus setup claude     (or: agentbus setup codex)\r\n  agentbus watch            (a live view for you; q quits)\r\n",
